id: pm-4f1l7f
title: Count successful provenance resolutions so historical health advisories can clear
description: "GitHub #1269 reports that successful resolver events omit agent_provenance_outcomes while health counts attempts and successes only from those outcomes, leaving old zero-success warnings after resolver repairs."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-18T04:33:51.530Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-18T04:33:51.530Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Cover failed-then-resolved, genuinely all-failed, unavailable-only and incomplete or bounded-history samples; verify through real SDK mutation and health flows, not fabricated success-only history."
parent: pm-5oj5
severity: medium
repro_steps: Use a workspace with historical failed resolver outcomes followed by successful probe-sourced model/version events. Inspect health zero-success warnings and compare successful event provenance with context.agent_provenance_outcomes.
expected_result: Successful probe resolutions must contribute truthful success evidence; repaired resolvers must not retain a permanent zero-success advisory. Expose the sampled measurement window and preserve real all-failure warnings.
actual_result: Reporter observes seven old failures and zero counted successes despite hundreds of newer successful probe records. Independent reproduction remains pending.
affected_version: 2026.9.17
component: SDK provenance health and immutable outcome recording
